From: Ubuntu gts9uwifi port contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: avoid a second video rotation on SM-X910

The SM-X910 software ISP already delivers screen-native buffers. Preserve the
orientation behaviour of the Noble camera SPA when building PipeWire 1.6.2.
The other six Noble PipeWire backports are present upstream or need separate
assessment; this patch is deliberately specific to the Resolute source.
---
 spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-source.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-source.cpp b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-source.cpp
--- a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-source.cpp
+++ b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-source.cpp
@@ -1233,7 +1233,7 @@
 		b->videotransform = (struct spa_meta_videotransform*)spa_buffer_find_meta_data(
 			buffers[i], SPA_META_VideoTransform, sizeof(*b->videotransform));
 		if (b->videotransform) {
-			b->videotransform->transform =
-				libcamera_orientation_to_spa_transform_value(impl->config->orientation);
+			/* SM-X910 software ISP buffers are already screen-native. */
+			b->videotransform->transform = SPA_META_TRANSFORMATION_None;
 			spa_log_debug(impl->log, "Setting videotransform for buffer %u to %u",
 				i, b->videotransform->transform);
